;; og:preserve-this tracker rung: landed from a scoped decode against this
;; worktree's own corrected all-types.gc (light-trail-tracker's own note
;; there carries the full slot-assignment-rule evidence trail: block order
;; alone decides real ids, jakx's process has one more inherited method than
;; jak3's so every real slot here is jak3's own number plus 1). tracking and
;; die are declared states (:virtual #t, real slots 15 and 16) but their own
;; bodies do not decode clean (event/trans hit the same handle-dereference
;; wall documented on light-trail-tracker-init-by-other below) and stay held;
;; the five :methods entries are the ones this rung's scoped decode content-
;; matched by body (see light-trails.gc for the landed four and the one held
;; slot).
;;
;; og:preserve-this decompwall rung: tracked-object retyped uint64 -> handle.
;; A scoped decode of should-draw? (real slot 20) showed the compiler's own
;; canonical sllv/lwu/dsra32 handle->process split reading this field
;; (machine offset 148, declared 152 per the +4 basics trap): op 5 (sllv a0,
;; v1, r0) extracts the low 32 bits as a process pointer, op 6 (l.wu 0(a0))
;; dereferences it, op 8 (dsra32 v1, v1, 0) extracts the pid for the
;; re-validation compare. The decompiler's own push_asm_sllv_to_stack
;; (decompiler/IR2/FormExpressionAnalysis.cpp) only folds this shift into a
;; real expression when the source register's type resolves to a bitfield
;; (collision-editor's own (proc) field, all-types.gc, is the exact same
;; class); declared uint64 here, it did not, and op 6's chained deref then
;; failed too ("Could not figure out load: (set! a0 (l.wu a0))"), producing
;; should-draw?'s own "Unsupported inline assembly instruction kind - [sllv
;; a0, v1, r0]". Retyping to handle (this field's own semantic type, per the
;; now-removed trailing comment) lets both ops resolve automatically. This is
;; the "same handle-dereference wall" the note above and light-trail-
;; tracker-init-by-other's own note below both cite; retire those two once
;; tracking/die and init-by-other are re-tried against this fix.
;;
;; og:preserve-this trailfinal rung: re-tried per the retirement note above.
;; light-trail-tracker-init-by-other retires clean (landed below, right
;; after tread-trail-tracker's own deftype). should-draw? and tracking/die do
;; NOT: their own re-derivation shows the retype fixed the SIMPLE fold shape
;; (a plain let-binding) but not this harder one. should-draw?'s fresh scoped
;; decode still carries an unresolved `.sllv a0, v1, r0` (this same op 5/6/8
;; triple, now embedded inside a nested and/or short-circuit chain the
;; decompiler's push_asm_sllv_to_stack pattern match does not reach), PLUS a
;; distinct new failure the retype does not touch: "failed type prop at 17:
;; Could not figure out load: (set! a2 (l.wu (+ a1 192)))", a field read on
;; the tracked PROCESS itself (a1 = the handle-derived pointer, not self)
;; that has no declared type at that offset. tracking's own :trans folds
;; clean now (same plain-let shape as init-by-other) but its :event does not:
;; a distinct, unrelated wall, "Expression building failed: In (event
;; tracking light-trail-tracker): Used float to int on a uint: (f2i f0-0)",
;; nothing to do with sllv or tracked-object. die decodes clean standalone
;; but posts to light-trail-tracker-common-post (light-trails.gc), itself
;; still held on should-draw?; landing die now would create the declared-
;; but-never-defined-symbol landmine this campaign's e2 class names. All
;; three (should-draw?, tracking, die) stay held; see light-trails.gc's own
;; trailfinal-rung note for weapon-trail-tracker/tread-trail-tracker's
;; tracking (same class, different offsets: 188 and 192) and the full
;; common-post chain.
;;
;; og:preserve-this trailcasts rung: should-draw? retires from the held
;; list above. Its own remaining wall was the fresh "Could not figure out
;; load: (set! a2 (l.wu (+ a1 192)))" this note's own trailfinal-rung
;; paragraph cites, a read of process-drawable's own draw field (raw 192,
;; declared 196, the +4 basics offset) on a1, the sllv fold's own output.
;; decompiler/config/jakx/ntsc_v1/type_casts.jsonc now carries a
;; "(method 20 light-trail-tracker)" entry narrowing a1 to process-drawable
;; at the four ops that read it (17/21/30/34), matching jak3's own already-
;; landed twin body's four (the-as process-drawable a1-0) casts
;; (goal_src/jak3/engine/gfx/sprite/particles/light-trails.gc's own
;; should-draw?) and jak3's own type_casts.jsonc entry for the same
;; function ("(method 19 light-trail-tracker)", jak3's own unshifted slot
;; number) on the identical four ops. The and/or nesting this note blamed
;; above was never the real blocker; the whole function's fold cascade was
;; downstream of the one unresolved load, and fixing the load resolves the
;; sllv fold too. should-draw? and light-trail-tracker-common-post both land
;; in light-trails.gc this rung (see that file's own trailcasts-rung note
;; for the full landing-order citation); tracking, die, and every
;; descendant's own tracking/hang-on state stay held, now solely on
;; common-trans!'s own unrelated integer-subtract wall against
;; expire-old-points!, out of this rung's scope.
(deftype light-trail-tracker (process)
  ((trail                light-trail  :offset-assert 144) ;; guessed by decompiler
   (tracked-object       handle       :offset-assert 152)
   (offscreen?           symbol       :offset-assert 160) ;; guessed by decompiler
   (offscreen-start-time uint64       :offset-assert 168) ;; time-frame
   (next-line-check-time uint64       :offset-assert 176) ;; time-frame
   (last-add-frame-val   uint32       :offset-assert 184)
   )
  :method-count-assert 22
  :size-assert         #xbc
  :flag-assert         #x16003000bc
  (:state-methods
    tracking ;; 15
    die ;; 16
    )
  (:methods
    (get-tracked-object-pos (_type_ process-focusable vector) vector) ;; 17
    (should-track? (_type_ process-focusable) symbol) ;; 18
    (should-end? (_type_ process-focusable) symbol) ;; 19
    (should-draw? (_type_) symbol) ;; 20
    (add-crumb! (_type_ vector) none) ;; 21
    )
  )

;; og:preserve-this tracker rung: weapon-trail-tracker installs its own
;; hang-on state at real slot 22 (this rung's scoped decode: `method-set!
;; weapon-trail-tracker 22 gp-4`), the first free slot after the parent's
;; corrected count of 22.
(deftype weapon-trail-tracker (light-trail-tracker)
  ((trail      weapon-trail :override)
   (joint0     int16        :offset-assert 188)
   (joint1     int16        :offset-assert 190)
   (state-time uint64       :offset-assert 192) ;; time-frame
   )
  :method-count-assert 23
  :size-assert         #xc8
  :flag-assert         #x17004000c8
  (:state-methods
    hang-on ;; 22
    )
  )

;; og:preserve-this tracker rung: tread-trail-tracker adds no new methods or
;; states; count and flag-assert follow the parent's corrected 22.
(deftype tread-trail-tracker (light-trail-tracker)
  ((trail tread-trail :override)
   )
  :method-count-assert 22
  :size-assert         #xbc
  :flag-assert         #x16003000bc
  )

;; og:preserve-this trailfinal rung: light-trail-tracker-init-by-other lands
;; from a fresh scoped decode against this worktree's own PR645 retype
;; (tracked-object: uint64 -> handle, on light-trail-tracker above). 0 ir2
;; markers, no ERROR banner: its own tracked-object read sits in a plain
;; (let ((gp-1 (handle->process ...)))) binding rather than a nested and/or
;; boolean chain, so the sllv/lwu/dsra32 fold fires cleanly here, unlike
;; should-draw? below (still held; its own fold still fails inside a deeper
;; boolean chain, see that note). Byte-identical in shape to jak3's own
;; landed twin (goal_src/jak3/engine/gfx/sprite/particles/light-trails-h.gc:
;; 217; only a cosmetic 0 vs (the-as uint 0) differs) and, per that same
;; twin, hosted in light-trails-h (this file), not light-trails.gc, matching
;; its two already-landed siblings weapon-trail-tracker-init-by-other and
;; tread-trail-tracker-init-by-other there. go-virtual tracking targets an
;; unfilled state slot, the same accepted shape those two siblings already
;; carry (tracking is still unlanded family-wide, held below and in
;; light-trails.gc). Every callee here (stack-size-set!, handle->process,
;; should-track?, add-crumb!, get-tracked-object-pos, setup!) is a real
;; already-landed definition or a compile-time macro, never a virtual-slot
;; or extern-only reference, so landing this carries no e2 risk.
;;
;; ARMING CHECK: this function's only caller anywhere in the corpus is
;; wvehicle-weapons-proj's mine-a/mine-b trail spawn, "(anon-function 59
;; wvehicle-weapons-proj)"/"(anon-function 99 wvehicle-weapons-proj)" per
;; decompiler/config/jakx/ntsc_v1/stack_structures.jsonc's own note on the
;; light-trail-tracker-spawn-params stack struct. Both anon-functions live
;; inside mine-a's and mine-b's own idle/falling state bodies, which stay
;; unlanded (goal_src/jakx/levels/common/wvehicle-weapons-proj.gc's own
;; rung-5 note: only mine-a-method-62/mine-b-method-65 are landed there).
;; Landing light-trail-tracker-init-by-other here does NOT arm the mine-trail
;; spawn path this rung; no landed caller reaches it yet.
(defbehavior light-trail-tracker-init-by-other light-trail-tracker ((arg0 light-trail-tracker-spawn-params))
  (stack-size-set! (-> self main-thread) 32)
  (set! (-> self tracked-object) (-> arg0 tracked-obj))
  (set! (-> self trail) (new 'process 'light-trail))
  (set! (-> self next-line-check-time) (the-as uint 0))
  (set! (-> self last-add-frame-val) (the-as uint 0))
  (set! (-> self offscreen?) #f)
  (setup! (-> self trail) (-> arg0 appearance) (-> arg0 max-num-crumbs))
  (when (-> arg0 track-immediately?)
    (let ((gp-1 (handle->process (-> self tracked-object))))
      (if (should-track? self (the-as process-focusable gp-1))
          (add-crumb!
            (-> self trail)
            (get-tracked-object-pos self (the-as process-focusable gp-1) (new 'stack-no-clear 'vector))
            (seconds 10000)
            )
          )
      )
    )
  (go-virtual tracking)
  )

